-- title:
--   Powers of vanishing germs lie in (σ₁varpiₜ,X₀,X₁)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero, and an intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq L((t))$ (the Laurent series field over $L$). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring which is an $A$-algebra domain with fraction field $L$, with $q \in \mathfrak m_A$, let $K$ carry an $A$-algebra structure making $A \to L \to K$ a scalar tower, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$. Write $\mathfrak X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout in schemes of the two maps $X_{\mathrm{Mid}} \to X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$, $X_{\mathrm{Mid}} \to X_{\mathrm{Inf}}$, where $X_{\mathrm{Fin}} = \operatorname{Spec} C$ with $C =$ `chartAlgFin A K j` the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Let $z \in \mathfrak X$ be the image of a point $y' \in \operatorname{Spec} C$ under $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$. Let $W_1$ be a complete discrete valuation ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal, with a ring map $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ such that $\mathfrak m_{W_1} = (\sigma_1 \varpi)$; let $f_1, u_1, v_1 \in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $f_1 \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, and let $e_1$ be a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak m_z$-adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ onto $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1})v_1 - f_1u_1)$. Then there exists $n \ge 1$ such that for every $a \in C$ lying in the prime $y'$, the image of $a$ in $S$ — formed by taking the germ at $z$ of $a$ regarded as a section over the open image $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(\top)$ via the identifications $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} C) \cong C$ and $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}^{\sharp}$, then passing to the completion and applying $e_1$ — has its $n$-th power in the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $\sigma_1 \varpi_t$, $X_0$ and $X_1$.
--
--   The statement records that functions on the finite chart vanishing at the chosen point become, after completion and transport along a Drinfeld-shaped presentation of the completed stalk, elements some power of which lies in the weighted centre $(\sigma_1\varpi_t, X_0, X_1)$; this is the radicality input needed to blow up the supersingular chart along that centre. It is used in the analysis of the blow-up chart of the auxiliary-level modular curve, in particular in the results on transitivity and reducedness of the primes of the blow-up chart and on points avoiding the Igusa-valuation orbit poles.
